@startuml sequence-diagram
title Simple Sequence Diagram - One Simulation Run

actor User
participant "Web UI" as UI
participant "Python Server" as Server
participant "C++ Simulator" as Simulator
participant NumericSeverity as Scoring
participant "Two Monitoring Threads" as Threads
participant ThreatDetector as Detector
participant Incident
participant SecurityReport as Report

User -> UI : run full demo or submit portal event
alt full demonstration
  UI -> Server : GET /api/run?scenario=...
else login or network portal event
  UI -> Server : POST /api/portal
  Server -> Server : validate event fields
end
Server -> Simulator : execute safe argument list

Simulator -> Scoring : calculate event severity
Scoring --> Simulator : score 1..5

alt invalid event
  Simulator -> Simulator : throw and catch custom exception
  Simulator -> Simulator : log validation error
else valid events
  Simulator -> Threads : start both workers
  Threads -> Threads : update metrics with mutex
  Threads --> Simulator : join and return totals
  Simulator -> Detector : evaluate rules and patterns
  Detector --> Simulator : threats and risk levels
  Simulator -> Incident : add alert, evidence and responses
  Incident --> Simulator : contained / failed outcomes
end

Simulator -> Report : generate summary
Report --> Simulator : risk and log totals
Simulator --> Server : console output
Server --> UI : JSON result
UI --> User : dashboard, comparison and evidence
@enduml
